# Button
# Level 1 - Basics
#
# The LED is on while you hold the button down.
# You learn: 'as input pullup' and read().
# You need: a pushbutton between pin 2 and GND. The pull-up inside the board means no resistor is needed.

board uno

led    = pin LED as output
button = pin 2 as input pullup     # reads true while the button is pressed

every 10 ms:
    led.write(button.read())       # the LED copies the button
